  "content": {
    "id": "p18-q5-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "5",
    "prompt": "Find the value of $a$ by simplifying the LHS so that each equation holds for all permissible values of $x$.",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 2,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p18-q5-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$$\\frac{a}{x-1}-\\frac2{x+1}=\\frac4{(x-1)(x+1)}$$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$a=2$",
          "worked": "For $x\\ne1,-1$,\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{a}{x-1}-\\frac2{x+1}&=\\frac{a(x+1)-2(x-1)}{(x-1)(x+1)}\\\\&=\\frac{(a-2)x+a+2}{(x-1)(x+1)}\\end{align*}$$\nCompare the numerator with $4$:\n$$\\begin{align*}a-2&=0\\\\a&=2\\end{align*}$$\nThen $a+2=4$, as required.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 54
      },
      {
        "id": "p18-q5-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$$\\frac3{2x-1}+\\frac{a}{x+1}=\\frac{5x+2}{(2x-1)(x+1)}$$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$a=1$",
          "worked": "For $x\\ne\\frac12,-1$,\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac3{2x-1}+\\frac{a}{x+1}&=\\frac{3(x+1)+a(2x-1)}{(2x-1)(x+1)}\\\\&=\\frac{(3+2a)x+3-a}{(2x-1)(x+1)}\\end{align*}$$\nCompare the numerator with $5x+2$:\n$$\\begin{align*}3+2a&=5\\\\a&=1\\end{align*}$$\nThen $3-a=2$, as required.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 54
      }
    ]
  },
